    "id": "train-1011",
    "question": "A carpenter is building a house. He needs 80 woodblocks to build it. If he has 8 logs that can make five woodblocks each, how many logs does the carpenter still need?",
    "gold": "8",
    "answer": "The carpenter initially has 8 x 5 = <<8*5=40>>40 blocks of wood.\nSo he still lacks 80 - 40 = <<80-40=40>>40 blocks of wood.\nTherefore he still needs 40 / 5 = <<40/5=8>>8 logs of wood.\n#### 8"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many logs the carpenter still needs, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of woodblocks that can be made from the 8 logs.\n2. Determine how many more woodblocks are needed after using the 8 logs.\n3. Calculate how many additional logs are required to get the necessary number of woodblocks.\n\nFirst, we know that each log can make 5 woodblocks. Therefore, 8 logs can make:\n\\[ 8 \\text{ logs} \\times 5 \\text{ woodblocks/log} = 40 \\text{ woodblocks} \\]\n\nThe carpenter needs a total of 80 woodblocks. Since he can already make 40 woodblocks with the 8 logs, he still needs:\n\\[ 80 \\text{ woodblocks} - 40 \\text{ woodblocks} = 40 \\text{ woodblocks} \\]\n\nNext, we need to find out how many logs are required to make 40 woodblocks. Since each log makes 5 woodblocks, the number of logs needed is:\n\\[ \\frac{40 \\text{ woodblocks}}{5 \\text{ woodblocks/log}} = 8 \\text{ logs} \\]\n\nTherefore, the carpenter still needs \\(\\boxed{8}\\) logs.",
